; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Teach the Turtle a New Word
; CATEGORY: Classic Logo
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     DEFINE, procedures, RUN, CATCH, interactive
; SUMMARY:  You type a name and some commands, and the program teaches them to Logo as a brand new procedure with DEFINE.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Asks you for the name of a new word, then for the turtle commands
;   that the word should mean. It tries the commands, and if they work
;   it uses DEFINE to make a real Logo procedure with that name. Then
;   it draws your new word three times in a row, so you can see it is
;   now part of the language.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and answer in the command center, for example:
;     name:      zigzag
;     commands:  repeat 3 [rt 45 fd 30 lt 90 fd 30 rt 45]
;   Type quit (or press Enter on an empty line) to stop. Your new
;   words stay defined, so afterwards you can type  zigzag  yourself.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a procedure is really just a name plus a list of instructions
;   * DEFINE builds a procedure from lists while the program runs
;   * CATCH "ERROR keeps a mistake from stopping the whole program
;   * RUN carries out a list of instructions
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Teach a word that uses another word you taught before.
;   * Type  po "zigzag  (PRINTOUT) to see the procedure you made.
;   * Make the program ask for an input, like :size, for the new word.
; ============================================================

; Seymour Papert liked to say that in Logo the child teaches the
; computer, rather than the other way round. Every TO ... END teaches
; Logo a new word. This program makes that idea very concrete: the
; words you invent here become real procedures, the same as if you had
; typed TO ... END in the editor.

to ask.name
  print []
  print [What new word shall we teach the turtle? Type quit to stop.]
  localmake "name readword
  if emptyp :name [output "quit]
  if memberp :name [quit bye stop exit] [output "quit]
  ; The name must be one plain word that is not a number and not
  ; already a Logo primitive (we cannot teach FORWARD a new meaning).
  if numberp :name [print [A number cannot be a new word. Try a name like zigzag.] output ask.name]
  if memberp "| | :name [print [Just one word please, with no spaces.] output ask.name]
  if primitivep :name [print (sentence :name [is already a Logo word. Pick another.]) output ask.name]
  ; and not one of this program's own procedures, or it would break itself
  if memberp :name [ask.name ask.commands show.off teach] [
    print [That word is part of this program. Pick another.] output ask.name]
  output :name
end

; Ask for commands until they run without an error. A bad answer
; prints Logo's own error message, which is a good hint.
to ask.commands :name :tries
  if :tries = 0 [output []]
  print (sentence [What should] :name [mean? Type turtle commands, like  fd 50 rt 90])
  localmake "body readlist
  if emptyp :body [output []]
  if memberp first :body [quit bye stop exit] [output []]
  clean penup home pendown
  catch "error [run :body output :body]
  print (sentence [Hmm, the turtle could not do that:] item 2 error)
  output ask.commands :name :tries - 1
end

; Show the new word three times along a line, so you see it is reusable.
to show.off :name
  clean
  foreach [-250 0 250] [
    penup setxy ? 0 setheading 0 pendown
    setpencolor item 1 + random 4 [[220 60 60] [40 120 220] [40 160 80] [230 140 20]]
    run (list :name)
  ]
end

to teach
  localmake "name ask.name
  if equalp :name "quit [print [Thanks for teaching me!] stop]
  localmake "body ask.commands :name 5
  if emptyp :body [print [All right, let's stop here.] stop]
  define :name (list [] :body)
  print (sentence [Now the turtle knows] word :name ". [Here it is three times:])
  show.off :name
  teach
end

clearscreen
setpensize 3
; A word taught before you start, as an example.
define "triangle [[] [repeat 3 [forward 80 right 120]]]
print [I already know TRIANGLE. Watch!]
triangle
teach
